text:
Maya R: filing bug — on foldable (Galaxy Fold) when keyboard opens the bottom nav overlays table row expansion. repro: open device in folded mode, go to Deployments > Instances, tap row to expand, keyboard opens for search and the expanded panel gets pushed under bottom nav.

Zach Li: can repro. probably a z-index + viewport height calc issue. mobile-toolbar uses safe-area-inset and sets fixed bottom; the content container is using 100vh which doesn't account for keyboard. :thinking:

Toni Brooks: accessibility concern: when the row expands it's not in the focus order (keyboard users can't reach the expand button after the soft keyboard pushes layout). Also touch targets for row actions are 38px — should be 44px min.

Liam O'Connor: quick CSS suggestion that helped in a similar case:
```
.container {
  height: calc(var(--vh, 1vh) * 100 - var(--toolbar-height));
  overflow: auto;
}
@media (max-width: 720px) and (orientation: portrait) {
  .sidebar { position: fixed; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; transform: translateY(100%);} /* make sidebar a sheet on narrow/fold mode */
}
```
Maya R: nice. can we also make the row expansion anchor to the visible viewport (use element.scrollIntoView({block: 'nearest'})) when opening? that should avoid content getting hidden behind nav.

Zach Li: +1. Also propose we change token of empty-state copy on mobile from "No results" to "No results — try clearing filters" with an inline CTA so users don't assume broken query. small copy tweak and add aria-live="polite" for results container.

layout-bot: created ISSUE-4123 with repro video and proposed CSS patch. @Maya R assigned.

Toni Brooks: UX nit — collapse chevrons in table rows need explicit aria-labels, e.g., "expand row details" / "collapse row details". Also screen reader should announce when panel opens.

Maya R: thanks team — I'll attach the video, add the copy suggestion to the issue, and prototype the bottom-sheet sidebar option. aiming for canary next week. :rocket:
